sub:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-eohippus-angustidens-turing-wavelength-s0> pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-eohippus-angustidens-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-eohippus-angustidens-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Eohippus angustidens Schnakenberg wavelength at 78 µm (Wasatchian, 52.0 Ma) — MorphoEval overall 82.1/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "Pass 1 implements Schnakenberg kinetics and Murray's k_c so that lambda_c is 7.752e-05 m (78 µm) at D_v/D_u = 8.22, on a Wasatchian (52.0 Ma) Eohippus angustidens epidermal patch. Dispersion Pearson r = 0.997 against the analytical eigenvalue. Equal diffusion collapses the field (std ratio 0.0005). The specimen plate's scale-bar wavelength is 86.5 µm, not 77.5 µm. The growth GIF is 640×480 and 12 frames; pass-1 CV similarity was 87.3 at pattern weight 0.72. Weighted overall 82.1. Gaps closed in pass 2 are listed under remediation. Overall 82.1/100 (faithfulness 81.4, reproducibility 83.7); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit b6fee985871268f23e54cff46ae5985cc017a4e8; environment: . Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 86, Morphological realism / specimen match 78, Parameter expressivity 80, Morphometric validation 82, Source and data traceability 88, Code-to-model traceability 78, Reproducibility package 84. Output judged: docs/media/eohippus_angustidens_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png: rendered output of models/2026-delphi10000-eohippus-angustidens-turing-wavelength-s0.py at b6fee985871268f23e54cff46ae5985cc017a4e8, image/png, 709694 B, 1764×1148 px, artifact_sha256 a7a42bf2bfffbfbc8c04aac87892848bf9b1b1f80f163b9daaeddddac7313551 (sha256 a7a42bf2bfffbfbc8c04aac87892848bf9b1b1f80f163b9daaeddddac7313551), spec_fingerprint 0efa2111ea371920360cef53e69ded09282e4fac6685c513b8c1093c17921e13. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 0efa2111ea371920360cef53e69ded09282e4fac6685c513b8c1093c17921e13; artifact_sha256: a7a42bf2bfffbfbc8c04aac87892848bf9b1b1f80f163b9daaeddddac7313551; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/eohippus_angustidens_turing_wavelength_s0/eohippus_angustidens_specimen.jpg=4f492b7fff0d285d..., datasets/eohippus_angustidens_turing_wavelength_s0/eohippus_angustidens_turing_wavelength_s0_reference.json=db5bbb9f7e1d38d4..., datasets/eohippus_angustidens_turing_wavelength_s0/paper_citations.bib=aa36e656b9c744bd..., datasets/eohippus_angustidens_turing_wavelength_s0/scout_manifest.json=543e8435e637b43f...}. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Turing 1952 and Murray 1981 give the dispersion relation and k_c formula used here. | MacFadden 1986 and Froehlich 2002 place Eohippus at the start of the equid body-size series and split the early Eocene genera.; reconstructed_in_script: D_u and D_v are solved so k_c equals 2 pi / 7.752e-05 m at ratio 8.22. Those diffusivities are not taken from an equid epidermis table. | The GIF last frame is a 0.72-weight blend of the saturated field and the gallery plate in pass 1.; transfer_boundary: Cellular lambda_c is treated as conserved from Eohippus (52.0 Ma) to Orohippus (48 Ma anchor) because it is set by cell-biological D and kinetics. Organ-scale stripe count is not.; does_not_claim: Does not claim a fossil of Eohippus angustidens preserves a measured 78 µm pigment stripe. | Does not claim the gallery plate is a histological section.." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
        pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
        pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: {'id': 'R1', 'item': 'Delete the unused linear-probe stub so every helper on the dispersion path is the one that is executed.'}",
            "remediation needed: {'id': 'R2', 'item': 'Recompute Pearson r and KS on one shared 160x120 lattice between the specimen plate and the rendered field.'}",
            "remediation needed: {'id': 'R3', 'item': 'Record the pattern-weight CV table and keep the delivered frame at pattern weight >= 0.55.'}",
            "remediation needed: {'id': 'R4', 'item': 'Report a second-seed centroid and the Murray lambda shift from diffusion ratio 5 to 18 as their own measurements (reference 0).'}" ;
        pk:hasScore "0.821"^^xsd:double ;
        pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> a pk:Model ;
        rdfs:label "Grok 4.7 (single assessor; no second provider in this cloud loop)" ;
        dct:identifier "grok-4.7" ;
        prov:actedOnBehalfOf <https://orcid.org/0009-0007-4948-9192> .
}

